      "number": 87,
      "shortId": "RF8FR",
      "priority": 1,
      "shortName": "verify-nerdfont-license",
      "title": "Verify Nerd Font license",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "Verificare la licenza della font usata per i glyph Nerd Font.\n\n## Answered (2026-07-30, F003/P085/T358)\n\nThe Nerd Font the app uses for glyphs is the one it **already ships**: `heca-renderer/assets/MapleMonoNormal-NF-Regular.ttf` (+ the Bold face), embedded as the default terminal face long before this phase. Its licence sits beside it — `heca-renderer/assets/MAPLE-OFL.txt`, **SIL Open Font License 1.1**, which permits embedding and redistribution in a binary.\n\nSo there is nothing to re-verify unless a **second**, different Nerd Font is introduced — which T090 deliberately avoided by reusing this one.",
      "notes": "",
