    },
    {
      "id": "adce30df-62ce-4a23-900a-097fec336df5",
      "phaseId": "36628b50-a0b5-4974-852e-96d68c09f11f",
      "number": 98,
      "shortId": "EJMNW",
      "priority": 3,
      "shortName": "embed-nerdfont-ranges",
      "title": "Embed Nerd Font glyph ranges",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "Embedding dei range di glyph usati.\n\n## Reconsidered (2026-07-30, F003/P085/T358)\n\n**Nothing new needs embedding today.** The app already ships a full Nerd Font — Maple Mono Normal NF, the default terminal face — loaded unconditionally at renderer init (`heca-renderer/src/text.rs`) and now addressed by family name for chrome glyphs too (`font::NERD_FONT_FAMILY`, `FontRole::NerdFont`). Every glyph `NfGlyph` names was verified present in its `cmap`.\n\nSo this task is really about **subsetting**, not embedding: the face carries ~12k codepoints and the app uses a handful outside the terminal. That is a binary-size question to answer on its own evidence (how much of it the terminal itself needs — a terminal genuinely wants the whole NF range, which may leave nothing to strip), not a prerequisite for `NfIcon`.\n\nWhoever picks this up: measure first, and check whether subsetting the terminal face breaks a user's powerline/devicon prompt before touching anything.",
      "notes": "",
